    description: "FOUND 2026-09-26 reading back INV-guzuj's fix (PR #1228). Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/guzuj_09262026/ (A/B surveys, diff.py, samples).\n\nA bare Go call to a function of the CALLER'S OWN PACKAGE is withheld by the resolver's ambiguity guard whenever the name has several candidates repo-wide, and since INV-guzuj it is emitted as the `external` placeholder (go:external:0-0:<name>:unresolved). Before INV-guzuj it emitted nothing. Measured: alertmanager +124 such placeholders, beads +379. All 16 sampled sites are same-package calls: New(...) in notify/<provider>/*_test.go calling that provider's New, newTestStore(...) and runGit(...) in beads test helpers, NewAlerts(...) in provider/mem.\n\nWHY IT IS RESOLVABLE. Go scoping answers a bare identifier call exactly: a name in the caller's own package, a builtin, or a dot import. No other package can be meant. So the caller's package directory is a path hint the resolver is not being given, and `external` is a sentinel standing in for a fact the analyzer holds (ADR-0051's objection to sentinels).\n\nNOT DONE: how the resolver scopes candidates by package directory, whether test files (package x_test) need the external-test-package rule, and the corpus frequency beyond these two repos."  # 63df
    fields: {}  # 63df
- op: discuss  # e0b4
