  nonce: e0b4  # e0b4
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES (the gap is wider than filed).\nCode: go.py bare-identifier arm (~go.py:3997-4180). local_symbols is per FILE; a same-package callee in another file goes to resolver.lookup(callee_name, path_hint=import_path_hint) with import_path_hint=None (go.py:4011) -- the caller's package directory is never offered. ListNameResolver (symbol_resolution.py:805) is built with ambiguity_threshold=3 (go.py:3275). INV-guzuj's arm (91d63993a9) emits make_unresolved_edge for the withheld name. go.py unchanged in this respect since filing.\nLive repro (analyze_go, scratch module; packages a/, b/, c/ each define New(); a/use.go, a/a_test.go, b/use.go call bare New()):\n  3 candidates: all three calls -> go:external:0-0:New:unresolved (the filed behaviour).\n  Same fixture WITHOUT c/ (2 candidates): b/use.go UseB -> go:a/a.go:3-3:New:function, confidence 0.57. A WRONG-PACKAGE bind: below the threshold the resolver returns the path-sorted first candidate (symbol_resolution.py, \"Ambiguous -- scale confidence by 1/sqrt(N)\").\nProposed update: the same missing hint causes BOTH halves -- external at N>=3, a wrong edge at N=2 (when the caller's package sorts later). The fix (caller's package dir as the hint, exact-package filter) closes both; the acceptance test should include the N=2 wrong-bind case, which is the finding-generating direction. The title/statement cover only the first half.\nNot re-measured: alertmanager 124 / beads 379. Not checked: package x_test (external test package) handling; go.mod-module-root vs directory identity for a package."  # e0b4
- op: update  # b347
  at: '2026-10-01T01:35:08Z'  # b347
  by: agent  # b347
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b347
  clock: 3  # b347
  nonce: b347  # b347
  set:  # b347
    title: "go: a bare call to a same-package function is resolved without the caller's package -- external placeholder at 3+ candidates (alertmanager 124, beads 379), WRONG-PACKAGE bind at 2 (confidence 0.57)"  # b347
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-26 reading back INV-guzuj's fix (PR #1228, 91d63993a9). Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/guzuj_09262026/ (A/B surveys, diff.py, samples).\n\nA bare Go call to a function of the CALLER'S OWN PACKAGE, defined in another file of that package, is looked up without the one fact Go scoping supplies. In go.py's bare-identifier arm, `local_symbols` covers the caller's own FILE only; anything else goes to `resolver.lookup(callee_name, path_hint=import_path_hint)` with `import_path_hint=None` (go.py:4011). The resolver is `ListNameResolver(global_symbols, ambiguity_threshold=3)` (go.py:3275; symbol_resolution.py:805). Two outcomes, both wrong:\n\n1. THREE OR MORE candidates repo-wide: the ambiguity guard withholds the bind and, since INV-guzuj, the call is emitted as the `external` placeholder (go:external:0-0:<name>:unresolved). Before INV-guzuj it emitted nothing. Measured at filing: alertmanager +124 such placeholders, beads +379 (not re-measured 2026-09-30). All 16 sampled sites are same-package calls: New(...) in notify/<provider>/*_test.go calling that provider's New, newTestStore(...) and runGit(...) in beads test helpers, NewAlerts(...) in provider/mem.\n\n2. EXACTLY TWO candidates: below the threshold the resolver returns the path-sorted FIRST candidate at confidence 1/sqrt(2) * 0.80 = 0.57. When the caller's package sorts later, that is a WRONG-PACKAGE edge. Live repro (2026-09-30, analyze_go, scratch module with packages a/ and b/ each defining New(), b/use.go calling bare New()): `UseB -> go:a/a.go:3-3:New:function`, confidence 0.57. Adding a third package c/ with New() turns all three calls into the external placeholder (case 1).\n\nCase 2 is the finding-generating direction (a call edge into a package the code never calls); case 1 is a recall loss.\n\nWHY IT IS RESOLVABLE. Go scoping answers a bare identifier call exactly: a name in the caller's own package, a builtin, or a dot import. No other package can be meant. So the caller's package directory is a hint the resolver is not being given, and both the `external` sentinel and the arbitrary first-candidate pick stand in for a fact the analyzer holds (ADR-0051's objection to sentinels).\n\nACCEPTANCE: a bare call resolves to the candidate in the caller's own package directory, and a candidate in any other package is never chosen for a bare call -- for N=2 (no wrong-package edge) and N>=3 (no external placeholder when the own package defines the name).\n\nNOT DONE: how the resolver scopes candidates by package directory (directory vs go.mod-module-relative identity), whether test files (package x_test, the external test package) need the external-test-package rule, and the corpus frequency beyond these two repos, including the case-2 count.\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # b347
